{"subject":"Microbiology","sourceTitle":"All In One Online","title":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","deckName":"created by tele @Neet_pg_bot::cereb::subject_tests::cereb sub test BTR::056-Extra-edge BTR test_ Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","questions":[{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192852","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":1,"stemHtml":"The following phenomenon not be observed in?<br/><img src=\"images/image_367_12_1.jpg\"/>","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bacillus anthracis"},{"label":"B","text":"Klebsiella pneumoniae"},{"label":"C","text":"Neisseria gonorrheae"},{"label":"D","text":"Hemophilus influenzae"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Neisseria gonorrheae","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans.</strong></span><strong> </strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>C) Neisseria gonorrheae</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192854","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":2,"stemHtml":"Which of the following stains are used to visualize the specific fibers present in the following cartilage?<br/><img src=\"https://cerebellum-web-static.s3.amazonaws.com/media/public/Screenshot%202025-06-07%20095425.jpg\"/>","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bielchowsky stain"},{"label":"B","text":"Verhoeff's stain"},{"label":"C","text":"GMS Silver stain"},{"label":"D","text":"Alcian Blue stain"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Verhoeff's stain","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. B) Verhoeff's stain</strong></span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\">The image shows elastic cartilage, identified by the presence of densely packed chondrocytes and a matrix containing elastic fibers. Verhoeff’s stain is specifically used to visualize elastic fibers, turning them black and allowing for detailed study of their distribution in tissues like elastic cartilage.</span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Other Option:</strong></span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Option A. Bielchowsky stain</strong>: Used for nerve fibers.</span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><img height=\"426\" src=\"https://cerebellum-web-static.s3.amazonaws.com/media/public/image_ICqPIBT.png\" width=\"536\"/></span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Option C.</strong> <strong>GMS silver stain: </strong>Used for fungi.</span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><img height=\"440\" src=\"https://cerebellum-web-static.s3.amazonaws.com/media/public/image_qMk2SlA.png\" width=\"551\"/></span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Option D.</strong> <strong>Alcian Blue stain: </strong>Used for acidic mucopolysaccharides, not specifically elastic fibers.</span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><img height=\"426\" src=\"https://cerebellum-web-static.s3.amazonaws.com/media/public/image_V3N7XhZ.png\" width=\"597\"/></span></p><br/><img src=\"https://cerebellum-web-static.s3.amazonaws.com/media/public/image_ICqPIBT.png\"/><br/><img src=\"https://cerebellum-web-static.s3.amazonaws.com/media/public/image_qMk2SlA.png\"/><br/><img src=\"https://cerebellum-web-static.s3.amazonaws.com/media/public/image_V3N7XhZ.png\"/><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192856","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":3,"stemHtml":"Identify the staining method for a tissue biopsy of the painless ulcer shown below:<br/><img src=\"images/image_379_2_1.jpg\"/>","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Fontana's method"},{"label":"B","text":"Levaditi's method"},{"label":"C","text":"Castaneda's method"},{"label":"D","text":"Albert's method"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Levaditi's method","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. B) Levaditi's method </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192858","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":4,"stemHtml":"Which of the following will be used to sterilise the instrument used to treat the following injury?<br/><img src=\"images/marrow-ed8-microbiology-001-023-1.webp\"/>","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ethylene oxide"},{"label":"B","text":"Gamma rays"},{"label":"C","text":"Hydrogen peroxide"},{"label":"D","text":"Ultraviolet rays"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Hydrogen peroxide","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. C) Hydrogen peroxide</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192860","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":5,"stemHtml":"What is the temperature used for this method of sterilisation?<br/><img src=\"https://cerebellum-web-static.s3.amazonaws.com/media/public/Screenshot%202025-06-07%20095516.jpg\"/>","options":[{"label":"A","text":"121°C for 15 minutes"},{"label":"B","text":"140°C for 120 minutes"},{"label":"C","text":"129°C for 20 minutes"},{"label":"D","text":"160°C for 120 minutes"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"121°C for 15 minutes","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. A) 121°C for 15 minutes </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192862","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":6,"stem":"Which among the following is a low-level disinfectant?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Isopropyl alcohol"},{"label":"B","text":"Glutaraldehyde"},{"label":"C","text":"Hydrogen peroxide"},{"label":"D","text":"Benzalkonium chloride"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Benzalkonium chloride","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. D) Benzalkonium chloride </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192864","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":7,"stem":"Identify the cells that lack MHC class 1 antigen:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Platelets"},{"label":"B","text":"T lymphocytes"},{"label":"C","text":"NK cells"},{"label":"D","text":"Red blood cells"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Red blood cells","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. D) Red blood cells </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192866","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":8,"stem":"A 4-month-old baby was brought with history of recurrent infections in the past 4 months. On examination white patches were present in oral mucosa which could be scraped easily. Which of the following statements is false about this condition?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It has autosomal as well as X linked inheritance"},{"label":"B","text":"Adenosine deaminase enzyme is deficient"},{"label":"C","text":"Tonsils are present"},{"label":"D","text":"B-cell count may be normal"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Tonsils are present","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. C) Tonsils are present</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192868","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":9,"stem":"Which of the following is a pigment-producing species of mycobacteria?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"M. ulcerans"},{"label":"B","text":"M. scrofulaceum"},{"label":"C","text":"M. avium intracellulare complex"},{"label":"D","text":"M. xenopi"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"M. scrofulaceum","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. B) M. scrofulaceum </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192870","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":10,"stem":"A 25-year-old HIV/AIDS man presents with fever, headache, photophobia and neck rigidity since the last 2 days. What is the empirical therapy of choice for this patient?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cefepime + Vancomycin + Ampicillin"},{"label":"B","text":"Ceftriaxone + Vancomycin"},{"label":"C","text":"Isoniazid + Rifampicin + Pyrazinamide+ Ethambutol"},{"label":"D","text":"Liposomal amphotericin B + Fluorocytosine"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Cefepime + Vancomycin + Ampicillin","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. A) Cefepime + Vancomycin + Ampicillin   </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192872","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":11,"stem":"Which of the following mediators of inflammation is an example of a C-X-C chemokine?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Lipoxin LXA-4"},{"label":"B","text":"IL-8"},{"label":"C","text":"Lymphotactin"},{"label":"D","text":"Fractalkine"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"IL-8","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. B) IL-8</strong></span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\">IL-8 is a C-X-C chemokine that primarily attracts neutrophils to sites of inflammation.</span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Other Option:</strong></span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Option A. Lipoxin LXA-4: </strong>A lipid mediator that resolves inflammation, not a chemokine.</span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Option C. Lymphotactin: </strong>A C chemokine, attracts lymphocytes, not neutrophils.</span></p><p> </p><p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Option D. Fractalkine: </strong>A CX3C chemokine, involved in leukocyte adhesion and migration.</span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192874","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":12,"stem":"Identify the microaerophilic bacteria from the list: Positive CLO test. Gram-negative bacilli implicated in GBSGram-negative curved bacilli with 'fish-in-stream' appearance Bacteria showing 'mercury drop' colonies. LJ medium showing ruff, buff, tough colonies.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2 and 5"},{"label":"B","text":"3 and 4"},{"label":"C","text":"1 and 4"},{"label":"D","text":"1 and 2"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"1 and 4","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. C) 1 and 4   </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192876","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":13,"stem":"Which of the following is not a characteristic feature of EI Tor vibrio?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Resistant to El Tor phage V"},{"label":"B","text":"Intrinsic resistance to polymyxin B"},{"label":"C","text":"Voges-Proskauer test is positive"},{"label":"D","text":"Not susceptible to group IV phage"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Resistant to El Tor phage V","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. A) Resistant to El Tor phage V   </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192878","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":14,"stem":"Which of the following microbes is also referred to as Friedlander's bacillus?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Klebsiella pneumoniae"},{"label":"B","text":"Corynebacterium diphtheria"},{"label":"C","text":"Chlamydia trachomatis"},{"label":"D","text":"Mycoplasma pneumoniae"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Klebsiella pneumoniae","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. A) Klebsiella pneumoniae </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192880","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":15,"stem":"Identify morphology of coronavirus:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Naked helically symmetrical viruses"},{"label":"B","text":"Enveloped icosahedrally symmetrical viruses"},{"label":"C","text":"Enveloped helically symmetrical viruses"},{"label":"D","text":"Variably enveloped viruses with a complex symmetry"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Enveloped helically symmetrical viruses","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. C) Enveloped helically symmetrical viruses   </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192882","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":16,"stem":"Which of the following is a false statement regarding the serological tests of syphilis?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rapid plasma reagin test is a group specific treponemal test"},{"label":"B","text":"VDRL test is the test of choice for response to therapy"},{"label":"C","text":"VDRL is the test of choice for examining CSF"},{"label":"D","text":"Treponemal tests are likely to remain reactive even after adequate therapy"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Rapid plasma reagin test is a group specific treponemal test","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. A) Rapid plasma reagin test is a group specific treponemal test</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192884","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":17,"stem":"A 34-year-old man presents with a discharging wound post-operatively. Cultures reveal infection with MRSA. Which of the following is the gene implicated?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"MecA"},{"label":"B","text":"MecB"},{"label":"C","text":"MecC"},{"label":"D","text":"MecM"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"MecA","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans.</strong> <strong>A) MecA</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192886","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":18,"stem":"There is an outbreak of hepatitis A infection in a college hostel. Which of the following is false about this infection?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It does not cause hepatocellular carcinoma"},{"label":"B","text":"The incubation period is 2-6 weeks"},{"label":"C","text":"Caused by an enveloped ssRNA virus"},{"label":"D","text":"Case fatality rate is 0.1%"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Caused by an enveloped ssRNA virus","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. C) Caused by an enveloped ssRNA virus</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192888","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":19,"stemHtml":"A 25-year-old male presents with difficulty swallowing, hydrophobia, and aerophobia after being bitten by a bat. He develops spasms, agitation, and coma, eventually succumbing to respiratory failure. Histopathological examination of his brain is shown in the image. Which of the following best describes the viral genome of the pathogen?<br/><img src=\"https://cerebellum-web-static.s3.amazonaws.com/media/public/Screenshot%202025-06-07%20095813.jpg\"/>","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Double-stranded DNA, enveloped"},{"label":"B","text":"Single-stranded RNA, positive-sense, enveloped"},{"label":"C","text":"Single-stranded RNA, negative-sense, enveloped"},{"label":"D","text":"Single-stranded RNA, segmented, non-enveloped"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Single-stranded RNA, negative-sense, enveloped","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans.</strong> <strong>C) Single-stranded RNA, negative-sense, enveloped</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192890","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":20,"stem":"Which among the following is not a sexual spore?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Zygospore"},{"label":"B","text":"Sporangiophore"},{"label":"C","text":"Basidiospore"},{"label":"D","text":"Ascospore"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Sporangiophore","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. B) Sporangiophore</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192892","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":21,"stem":"A 22-year-old man comes with complaints of intermittent bloody diarrhea for 3 weeks after consuming street food during his travel. He is febrile and has RUQ tenderness. Which of the following is the infective form of the likely protozoan causing this disease?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Trophozoite"},{"label":"B","text":"Mature quadrinucleate cyst"},{"label":"C","text":"Metacyclic trophozoite"},{"label":"D","text":"Precyst"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Mature quadrinucleate cyst","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. B) Mature quadrinucleate cyst   </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192894","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":22,"stem":"Which of the following refers to a host in which the larval stage of the parasite remains viable without further development?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Definitive host"},{"label":"B","text":"Intermediate host"},{"label":"C","text":"Paratenic host"},{"label":"D","text":"Reservoir host"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Paratenic host","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. C) Paratenic host   </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192896","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":23,"stem":"A woman who came with complaints of fever, myalgia, and rash at 12 weeks of gestation is found to have positive IgM titers for rubella. She is advised MTP. If the pregnancy is taken to full term, which of the following triad of complications would you expect to see in the child?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Chorioretinitis, hydrocephalus, intracranial calcifications"},{"label":"B","text":"Sensorineural hearing loss, blueberry muffin rash, microcephaly"},{"label":"C","text":"Cataracts, cicatricial skin lesions, limb defects"},{"label":"D","text":"Sensorineural hearing loss, cataract, congenital heart defects"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Sensorineural hearing loss, cataract, congenital heart defects","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. D) Sensorineural hearing loss, cataract, congenital heart defects </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192898","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":24,"stem":"Which of the following statements about immunoglobulins is false?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"IgG is used to diagnose fetal infection"},{"label":"B","text":"IgM has weak precipitation activity"},{"label":"C","text":"IgG has four subclasses"},{"label":"D","text":"IgM is mainly intravascular"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"IgG is used to diagnose fetal infection","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. A) IgG is used to diagnose fetal infection </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192900","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":25,"stem":"Which of the following bones violates ‘The secondary ossification center that appears first, fuses last’ law?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Radius"},{"label":"B","text":"Fibula"},{"label":"C","text":"Ulna"},{"label":"D","text":"Sternum"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Fibula","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. B) Fibula </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192902","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":26,"stem":"Which among the following is wrong about the venous drainage of the heart?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Coronary sinus is guarded by the thebesian valve"},{"label":"B","text":"Middle cardiac vein lies in the posterior atrioventricular groove"},{"label":"C","text":"Great cardiac vein accompanies left anterior descending artery"},{"label":"D","text":"Anterior cardiac vein opens into RA directly"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Middle cardiac vein lies in the posterior atrioventricular groove","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. B) Middle cardiac vein lies in the posterior atrioventricular groove</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192904","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":27,"stem":"Which of the following types of joints is incorrectly matched?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Acromioclavicular joint – Plane synovial joint"},{"label":"B","text":"Wrist joint – Condyloid joint"},{"label":"C","text":"Sternoclavicular joint – Plane joint"},{"label":"D","text":"Intercarpal– Plane synovial joint"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Sternoclavicular joint – Plane joint","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. C) Sternoclavicular joint – Plane joint</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192906","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":28,"stem":"Which of the following properties of the eustachian tube predisposes to higher incidence of acute otitis media in children than adults?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"More angulated at isthmus"},{"label":"B","text":"Rigid cartilage"},{"label":"C","text":"Dense elastin in the cartilage"},{"label":"D","text":"Wider and shorter tube"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Wider and shorter tube","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. D) Wider and shorter tube</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192908","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":29,"stem":"You should not insert the needle below which level in midaxillary line so as not to damage the liver?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"6th rib"},{"label":"B","text":"10th rib"},{"label":"C","text":"8th rib"},{"label":"D","text":"12th rib"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"10th rib","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. B) 10th rib</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192910","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":30,"stem":"In which layer of the cerebral cortex is the outer band of Baillarger seen?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"External pyramidal layer"},{"label":"B","text":"Internal granular layer"},{"label":"C","text":"Internal pyramidal layer"},{"label":"D","text":"External granular layer"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Internal granular layer","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. B) Internal granular layer</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192912","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":31,"stem":"Arrange the following events of pre-embryonic development in order, from the earlier stage to the later stage: CavitationCompactionImplantationCleavage","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2 - 4 - 1 - 3"},{"label":"B","text":"3 - 1 - 2 - 4"},{"label":"C","text":"4 - 2 - 3 - 1"},{"label":"D","text":"4 - 2 - 1 - 3"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"4 - 2 - 1 - 3","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. D) 4 - 2 - 1 - 3</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192914","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":32,"stem":"Which of the following brainstem nuclei is not derived from the alar plate?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Inferior olivary"},{"label":"B","text":"Substantia nigra"},{"label":"C","text":"Dentate"},{"label":"D","text":"Hypoglossal"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Hypoglossal","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. D) Hypoglossal </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192916","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":33,"stem":"The membranous labyrinth develops from which structure?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"First pharyngeal pouch"},{"label":"B","text":"First pharyngeal cleft"},{"label":"C",