ing would be the sentinel lymph nodes?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Submandibular lymph nodes"},{"label":"B","text":"Submental lymph nodes"},{"label":"C","text":"Deep cervical lymph nodes"},{"label":"D","text":"Jugulo-omohyoid lymph nodes"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Submental lymph nodes","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. B) Submental lymph nodes</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192934","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":42,"stem":"Which of the following muscle causes opening of laryngeal inlet?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Vocalis"},{"label":"B","text":"Thyroepiglotticus"},{"label":"C","text":"Cricoarytenoid"},{"label":"D","text":"Thyroarytenoid"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Thyroepiglotticus","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. B) Thyroepiglotticus</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":"","stemHtml":"<p>Which of the following muscle causes opening of laryngeal inlet?</p><figure class=\"marrow-ed8-visual\"><img src=\"images/marrow-ed8-ent-034-021-1.webp\" alt=\"Marrow ED8 question visual from page 524\" loading=\"lazy\" /></figure><figure class=\"marrow-ed8-visual\"><img src=\"images/marrow-ed8-ent-034-021-2.webp\" alt=\"Marrow ED8 question visual from page 527\" loading=\"lazy\" /></figure><figure class=\"marrow-ed8-visual\"><img src=\"images/marrow-ed8-ent-034-021-3.webp\" alt=\"Marrow ED8 question visual from page 528\" loading=\"lazy\" /></figure>"},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192936","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":43,"stemHtml":"The artery passing through the structure marked A is a branch of which part of the maxillary artery?<br/><img src=\"https://cerebellum-web-static.s3.amazonaws.com/media/public/Screenshot%202025-06-07%20100042.jpg\"/>","options":[{"label":"A","text":"First part"},{"label":"B","text":"Second part"},{"label":"C","text":"Third part"},{"label":"D","text":"Fourth part"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Third part","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. C) Third part</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192938","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":44,"stem":"Which of the following muscles is not involved in the formation of the perineal body?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bulbospongiosus muscle"},{"label":"B","text":"Superficial transverse perineal muscles"},{"label":"C","text":"Deep transverse perineal muscles"},{"label":"D","text":"Internal anal sphincter muscle"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Internal anal sphincter muscle","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. D) Internal anal sphincter muscle </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192940","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":45,"stem":"Which of the following structures of the inguinal canal lies outside the internal spermatic fascia?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pampiniform plexus of veins"},{"label":"B","text":"Testicular artery"},{"label":"C","text":"Testicular nerve plexus"},{"label":"D","text":"Ilioinguinal nerve"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Ilioinguinal nerve","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. D) Ilioinguinal nerve </strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192942","topic":"Cerebellum · 056-Extra-edge BTR test Micro-Anat - 2025-06-07","number":46,"stem":"Which of the following muscles causes external rotation of the hip joint?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Gluteus medius"},{"label":"B","text":"Gluteus maximus"},{"label":"C","text":"Tensor fascia lata"},{"label":"D","text":"Adductor longus"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Gluteus maximus","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\"><strong>Ans. B) Gluteus maximus</strong></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436192944","t